1
00:00:02,569 --> 00:00:06,667
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:07,006 --> 00:00:08,943
Huh. Wow.

3
00:00:08,943 --> 00:00:11,602
A drop this deep really makes
you wonder about the necessity

4
00:00:11,602 --> 00:00:13,964
of having a chamber this size.

5
00:00:13,964 --> 00:00:16,712
It's just as well that
green goo is down there.

6
00:00:16,712 --> 00:00:20,665
If I thought it was water, I'd be tempted
to just jump off here and do a cannonball.

7
00:00:20,665 --> 00:00:23,571
I bet I could get a splash
two stories high.

8
00:00:23,571 --> 00:00:24,974
Is that a pixie?

9
00:00:24,974 --> 00:00:28,198
Science hasn't disproven
the existence of pixies.

10
00:00:28,198 --> 00:00:31,938
If they can shift through dimensions, that
would explain the lack of evidence for them.

11
00:00:31,938 --> 00:00:32,764
What's this?

12
00:00:32,764 --> 00:00:33,707
[lights clicking on]

13
00:00:33,707 --> 00:00:35,223
[lights clicking on]
I'm hearing clicking.

14
00:00:35,223 --> 00:00:36,843
[lights clicking on]
Pixies don't click.

15
00:00:36,843 --> 00:00:37,923
[lights clicking on]
Is that you?

16
00:00:37,923 --> 00:00:39,234
No. Hey, lights.

17
00:00:39,234 --> 00:00:40,665
What?  Who did the--?

18
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:43,126
[metallic rumbling]
Oh. Good!

19
00:00:43,126 --> 00:00:45,207
[metallic rumbling]
I can get out of here!

20
00:00:45,207 --> 00:00:47,878
[metallic rumbling]
Hey, wait. That's not a pixie.

21
00:00:47,878 --> 00:00:49,267
That's just some blue light.

22
00:00:50,209 --> 00:00:53,005
This whole place is built on deception.

23
00:00:53,005 --> 00:00:54,015
Screw it.

24
00:00:54,015 --> 00:00:55,267
Going up.

25
00:00:56,228 --> 00:00:57,962
No! Going up, dammit!

26
00:00:57,962 --> 00:00:59,263
That's where I came from!

27
00:00:59,263 --> 00:00:59,801
UP!

28
00:01:00,585 --> 00:01:02,184
Argh! This is going to take for--

29
00:01:02,184 --> 00:01:05,098
[metallic banging]

30
00:01:05,098 --> 00:01:07,301
I guess I spoke too soon.

31
00:01:07,301 --> 00:01:08,168
Uh.

32
00:01:08,168 --> 00:01:09,516
[metallic groaning]

33
00:01:09,516 --> 00:01:10,172
[metallic groaning]
Jesus!

34
00:01:10,172 --> 00:01:11,200
[metallic creaking]

35
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:13,132
[metallic creaking]
I don't like this...

36
00:01:13,132 --> 00:01:13,624
[metallic creaking]

37
00:01:13,624 --> 00:01:15,241
[metallic creaking]
Okay, I'm in a rickety-ass elevator

38
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:17,112
[metallic creaking]
that's creaking. What do I do?

39
00:01:17,112 --> 00:01:18,108
[metallic creaking]
Get off it?

40
00:01:18,108 --> 00:01:19,904
[metallic creaking]
Okay, that looks like a pipe.

41
00:01:19,904 --> 00:01:21,732
[metallic groaning]
Looks like it might go somewhere.

42
00:01:21,732 --> 00:01:24,001
[metallic groaning]
Don't think I have a lot of options.

43
00:01:24,001 --> 00:01:25,739
[metallic groaning]
Okay, I-I can jump this.

44
00:01:25,739 --> 00:01:26,694
[metallic groaning]
And the irony is,

45
00:01:26,694 --> 00:01:28,082
[metallic groaning]
it's probably going to be one of the safer

46
00:01:28,082 --> 00:01:29,592
[metallic groaning]
jumps I've done this morning.

47
00:01:29,592 --> 00:01:30,802
[metallic groaning]
Assuming I don't die.

48
00:01:30,802 --> 00:01:32,392
[metallic creaking]

49
00:01:32,392 --> 00:01:35,058
[electrical sparking, metallic banging]

50
00:01:35,058 --> 00:01:37,351
[electrical sparking, metallic banging]
Oh, man!

51
00:01:37,351 --> 00:01:39,559
I climbed my way to safety!

52
00:01:39,559 --> 00:01:42,441
I AM A MONKEY GOD!

53
00:01:42,441 --> 00:01:50,540
[monkey calls]

54
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:51,950
[Geiger counter clicks]

55
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:53,814
[Geiger counter clicks]
That could be me right now,

56
00:01:53,814 --> 00:01:56,072
[Geiger counter clicks]
a toxic human french fry.

57
00:01:56,072 --> 00:01:59,884
[Geiger counter clicks]
But no, my simian skills saw me safely.

58
00:01:59,884 --> 00:02:01,045
Hey, did you see that?

59
00:02:01,045 --> 00:02:02,350
SCIENTIST: I hope no one expects me
Look at me! Look at me!

60
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:05,251
SCIENTIST: to start up the generator.
Smithers went down there and

61
00:02:05,251 --> 00:02:06,670
SCIENTIST: never came back.

62
00:02:06,670 --> 00:02:08,274
Oh, you think he escaped?

63
00:02:08,274 --> 00:02:11,722
All right, here's the plan: you keep staring
at your dials and I'll get out of here.

64
00:02:11,722 --> 00:02:14,321
I mean, I wouldn't come back
for you if I found an exit.

65
00:02:14,321 --> 00:02:15,509
That's not my job.

66
00:02:15,509 --> 00:02:16,664
[Geiger counter clicks]

67
00:02:16,664 --> 00:02:18,409
[Geiger counter clicks]
Ah, tick-tick-tock.

68
00:02:18,409 --> 00:02:19,895
[Geiger counter clicks]
Is that the sound of a Geiger counter

69
00:02:19,895 --> 00:02:21,847
[Geiger counter clicks]
or is my lifespan counting down?

70
00:02:21,847 --> 00:02:23,061
[Geiger counter clicks]
It's both!

71
00:02:23,061 --> 00:02:24,908
[Geiger counter clicks]
That's right, here at Black Mesa,

72
00:02:24,908 --> 00:02:26,550
[Geiger counter clicks]
when we talk about half-life,

73
00:02:26,550 --> 00:02:28,425
[Geiger counter clicks]
we mean it more ways than one.

74
00:02:28,425 --> 00:02:29,403
[Geiger counter clicks]
So, make your peace and

75
00:02:29,403 --> 00:02:30,868
[Geiger counter clicks]
come to Black Mesa.

76
00:02:31,706 --> 00:02:34,381
Here, you'll win a chance to
fight freaks of nature,

77
00:02:34,381 --> 00:02:36,439
escape countless safety hazards,

78
00:02:36,439 --> 00:02:38,338
wander aimlessly for hours,

79
00:02:38,338 --> 00:02:41,149
[bullsquid spits]
and die scared, tired and alone.

80
00:02:41,149 --> 00:02:43,068
[bullsquid spits]
Where's that noise coming from?

81
00:02:43,068 --> 00:02:45,597
[bullsquid spits]
Yeah, I'm calling you out, noise.

82
00:02:45,597 --> 00:02:46,667
[bullsquid spits]
Oh, it's you.

83
00:02:47,136 --> 00:02:49,267
[bullsquid spits]
This is almost getting to be like a chore.

84
00:02:50,705 --> 00:02:52,290
Y'know, wash the dishes,

85
00:02:52,290 --> 00:02:53,397
do the laundry,

86
00:02:53,397 --> 00:02:54,762
shoot the snot thing,

87
00:02:54,762 --> 00:02:56,280
empty the trash...

88
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:58,250
It's all just a blur.

89
00:02:58,250 --> 00:02:59,234
What's this do?

90
00:02:59,711 --> 00:03:00,090
WHOA!

91
00:03:01,965 --> 00:03:03,234
Nnnnnnyyyeeeeow!

92
00:03:04,067 --> 00:03:06,167
That was awesome, let's do it again.

93
00:03:06,676 --> 00:03:10,230
[whistles]

94
00:03:11,203 --> 00:03:12,169
AGAIN!

95
00:03:12,169 --> 00:03:15,901
[whistles]

96
00:03:16,407 --> 00:03:17,328
AGAIN!

97
00:03:17,328 --> 00:03:18,887
Eh, no, better not.

98
00:03:18,887 --> 00:03:20,593
I could do this all day.

99
00:03:20,593 --> 00:03:23,934
I'm never going to rich enough to
buy my own island if I keep this up.

100
00:03:25,506 --> 00:03:26,067
Wow.

101
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:28,791
Yeah, it's like that experiment with rats,

102
00:03:28,791 --> 00:03:31,511
where every hour they're given
the choice between food

103
00:03:31,511 --> 00:03:34,110
or having the pleasure center of
their brain stimulated

104
00:03:34,110 --> 00:03:36,033
and the rats starve to death every time.

105
00:03:37,538 --> 00:03:38,000
Hup!

106
00:03:38,546 --> 00:03:41,860
You know, that first ride was fun but
this one looks kind of dangerous.

107
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:43,734
It's just slamming back and forth.

108
00:03:44,859 --> 00:03:47,330
Whoa-ho. Yeah, you can feel THAT passing.

109
00:03:47,330 --> 00:03:50,759
That'll knock your head off like
one of those little tee-ball sticks.

110
00:03:50,759 --> 00:03:54,067
That's snap, crackle, and pop
all in one package.

111
00:03:55,554 --> 00:03:56,567
Ah, a button.

112
00:03:58,244 --> 00:03:59,701
Well, my work here is done.

113
00:04:00,611 --> 00:04:02,176
Hey, are you a monkey, too?

114
00:04:02,176 --> 00:04:02,710
[monkey call]

115
00:04:02,710 --> 00:04:05,127
SMITHERS: This is my hiding
spot, and I'm not moving

116
00:04:05,127 --> 00:04:07,577
SMITHERS: until the situation
has drastically improved.

117
00:04:07,577 --> 00:04:10,210
SMITHERS: Now go away!
And don't tell anyone I'm here!

118
00:04:10,210 --> 00:04:13,394
Okay, I'm going to call you Mr. Fantastic.

119
00:04:13,394 --> 00:04:15,524
Or wait, no, Doc-Doctor Amazing.

120
00:04:15,524 --> 00:04:16,555
Doctor Amazing.

121
00:04:16,555 --> 00:04:17,167
Ah hah.

122
00:04:18,645 --> 00:04:20,033
Well, that was anticlimactic.

123
00:04:20,498 --> 00:04:23,714
I was hoping that some music would
start playing if I pressed both of them.

124
00:04:23,714 --> 00:04:27,694
Y'know, it would be cool if we could get
a dance party going on up here, like a rave?

125
00:04:27,694 --> 00:04:29,697
I bet the acoustics of this room
would be interesting.

126
00:04:29,697 --> 00:04:30,399
[boom]
SMITHERS: AAAH!

127
00:04:30,399 --> 00:04:30,939
What?!

128
00:04:30,939 --> 00:04:31,888
SMITHERS: OH DEAR!

129
00:04:31,888 --> 00:04:33,527
Man, you're not going to be missed.

130
00:04:33,527 --> 00:04:34,998
Nobody's going to come looking for you.

131
00:04:34,998 --> 00:04:35,538
[electrical humming and crackling]

132
00:04:35,538 --> 00:04:37,207
[electrical humming and crackling]
Uh...wait a minute.

133
00:04:37,207 --> 00:04:39,703
[electrical humming and crackling]
Okay, we're not electrocuted...

134
00:04:39,703 --> 00:04:41,727
[electrical humming and crackling]
I've determined that much...

135
00:04:41,727 --> 00:04:46,076
[electrical humming and crackling]
but... um... not seeing a way down... now...

136
00:04:46,076 --> 00:04:48,551
[electrical humming and crackling]
Umm... shit.

137
00:04:48,551 --> 00:04:49,658
[electrical humming and crackling]
I think I fucked up.

138
00:04:49,658 --> 00:04:50,550
[electrical humming and crackling]

139
00:04:50,550 --> 00:04:52,448
[electrical humming and crackling]
I think I fucked up, man.

140
00:04:52,448 --> 00:04:55,175
[electrical humming and crackling]
I... shouldn't... press buttons without...

141
00:04:55,175 --> 00:04:57,154
[electrical humming and crackling]
knowing what they do first...

142
00:04:57,154 --> 00:04:59,370
[electrical humming and crackling]
Oh, oh, okay.  We can get down--

143
00:04:59,370 --> 00:05:01,013
[electrical humming and crackling]
I mean, I can get down here.

144
00:05:01,013 --> 00:05:02,835
[electrical humming and crackling]
Okay, I'll just lower myself down

145
00:05:02,835 --> 00:05:04,268
[electrical humming and crackling]
and be careful about the landing.

146
00:05:04,268 --> 00:05:05,887
[electrical humming and crackling]

147
00:05:05,887 --> 00:05:09,088
[electrical humming and crackling]
Oooh... okay... um.... that's pretty scary...

148
00:05:09,088 --> 00:05:09,901
[electrical humming and crackling]
Yaaahh....!

149
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:14,133
God dammit, Earth's gravity shouldn't
even be this strong for a planet our size.

150
00:05:14,133 --> 00:05:15,972
It's only this way because there's
so many metals in the core

151
00:05:15,972 --> 00:05:17,233
increasing its overall density so that--

152
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:18,534
Oh fuck, I'm going to have to jump here.

153
00:05:20,868 --> 00:05:22,823
Okay, lower myself down...

154
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:24,868
to reduce the VERtical... drop...!

155
00:05:25,427 --> 00:05:28,694
Now, time it so I don't get
sideswiped by the cart of death...

156
00:05:28,694 --> 00:05:29,200
And...

157
00:05:30,131 --> 00:05:31,912
Aaagh... rrr...

158
00:05:31,912 --> 00:05:32,919
Okay...

159
00:05:32,919 --> 00:05:33,602
Yeah...

160
00:05:33,602 --> 00:05:36,033
I'm just going to take it easy.

161
00:05:36,801 --> 00:05:40,254
God, that would've been so
much easier if I was drunk.

162
00:05:40,254 --> 00:05:44,875
I mean, not piss-drunk, but
y'know, just like a heavy buzz.

163
00:05:44,875 --> 00:05:48,419
I would've been fearless,
wouldn't have hurt my knees at all.

164
00:05:48,419 --> 00:05:50,100
This sucks sober!

165
00:05:50,617 --> 00:05:52,367
Life sucks sober!

166
00:05:52,909 --> 00:05:57,145
Oh God oh God oh God
oh God oh God...oh God...

167
00:05:57,145 --> 00:06:02,962
Okay, I think coming this way
has the biggest waste of time

168
00:06:02,962 --> 00:06:04,868
I've accomplished in a while.

169
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:07,061
That's saying a lot.

170
00:06:07,061 --> 00:06:12,609
I mean it's not like I just went down
the wrong corridor, like I sometimes do.

171
00:06:12,609 --> 00:06:17,209
No, it's--WHEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE!

172
00:06:17,209 --> 00:06:18,604
It's worse than that.

173
00:06:18,604 --> 00:06:22,808
Hey, that looks kind of cool.
I want a giant metal spider fortress.

174
00:06:22,808 --> 00:06:24,221
What was I thinking about?

175
00:06:24,221 --> 00:06:26,102
Oh yeah, this place sucks.

176
00:06:26,102 --> 00:06:27,422
[Geiger counter clicks]
How could I forget?

177
00:06:27,422 --> 00:06:29,026
[Geiger counter clicks]
Yeah, when I go down a dead-end here,

178
00:06:29,026 --> 00:06:31,399
[Geiger counter clicks]
I go down a DEAD-END!

179
00:06:31,399 --> 00:06:33,986
[Geiger counter clicks]
Meaning, I go off course for, like, miles,

180
00:06:33,986 --> 00:06:37,792
[Geiger counter clicks]
ten stories underground, and I almost die.

181
00:06:37,792 --> 00:06:39,051
A lot.

182
00:06:39,051 --> 00:06:40,277
SCIENTIST: Excellent!
Yoo-hoo!

183
00:06:40,277 --> 00:06:42,543
SCIENTIST: Someone has restored all power.

184
00:06:42,543 --> 00:06:44,655
SCIENTIST: We'll have the engine
up again in no time!

185
00:06:44,655 --> 00:06:45,916
Yeah, that room's dangerous.

186
00:06:45,916 --> 00:06:46,860
Did you know that?

187
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:49,583
It's a good thing I made it back okay.

188
00:06:49,583 --> 00:06:53,576
I was gonna... yedduh... yes, master...

189
00:06:53,576 --> 00:06:54,774
No, stop!

190
00:06:54,774 --> 00:06:58,264
You can't kill me, so you're going
to try and control me, IS THAT IT!?!

191
00:06:58,264 --> 00:07:00,082
[Geiger counter clicks]
I'LL NEVER DO YOUR BIDDING!

192
00:07:00,082 --> 00:07:02,621
[Geiger counter clicks]
I HAVE A DOCTOR'S DEGREE!

193
00:07:02,621 --> 00:07:04,191
[Geiger counter clicks]
Wait, how am I going to get out of here?

194
00:07:04,191 --> 00:07:08,076
[Geiger counter clicks]

195
00:07:08,076 --> 00:07:10,539
[Geiger counter clicks]
I should've thought about this sooner...

196
00:07:10,539 --> 00:07:14,667
[Geiger counter clicks]

